From 8f0891eb453190568a28b0e51ff3b1bbaa5b0fc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CompuLab <support@compulab.co.il>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 19:22:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: edgedes: add tevs and framos imx678

Adapt the validated TechNexion TEVS sensor and native FRAMOS IMX678 RAW12
subset to the ADI v18 media graph on Linux 6.18. Sensor streaming controls
only the sensor; the parent ADI subdevices recursively control GMSL
streaming. Place sensors behind the ADI address translator instead of
using flat sensor nodes and TechNexion transport phandles.

Provide source-pad-0, stream-0 CSI-2 frame descriptors. TEVS reports its
selected pixel code and programmed VC, with standard UYVY/Y8 datatype.
IMX678 reports native RAW12 VC 0. Program standard YUV422 datatype 0x1e
in TEVS so its packets match the ADI descriptor and remap configuration.
Retain NVIDIA tegracam metadata and the existing vendor controls.

Initialize TEVS private controls and frame-interval operations before
async publication through the companion tegracam init_private_controls
hook. This prevents graph completion from copying an empty handler and
early capture from dereferencing uninitialized control pointers. Replace
the generic placeholder geometry with the detected module's defaults.

Preserve the proven FRAMOS reset sequence through generic GPIO consumers:
hold XCLR low and TENABLE low; optionally drive PW_EN_0 low for 5 ms and
then high; enable INCK; wait 200 ms; release XCLR; wait another 40 ms.
Use reset-gpios (active-low MFP0), optional tenable-gpios (active-high
MFP6), optional power-enable-gpios (active-high MFP8) and serializer MCLK.
Omit a consumer property if a serializer GPIO hog owns that line.

TEVS provenance: TechNexion tn-jetson-camera-driver branch
tn_l4t-r39.2.ga_kernel-6.8, commit
51ffafe6a7efc4fb21a39a067f5804783ac66d31, GPL-2.0, with validated CompuLab
R39 adaptations from the existing minimal camera patch.
FRAMOS provenance: framos-jetson-drivers l4t-r38.4 commit
d9890dedb5c32f651231f99c49e42ef78d728b12, GPL-2.0, through the existing
minimal native RAW12 patch. Vendor copyright/license notices and the
TechNexion GPL-2.0 license are preserved.

Requires the separate tegracam get_frame_desc and init_private_controls
callback integration patch. NVIDIA OOT builds these modules through
obj-m; the companion Kconfig records dependencies for a future in-tree
build.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [NVIDIA tegracam and CompuLab EDGEDES integration]
